{"base_rate":0.5444743935309974,"brier":0.27977628032345014,"bss":-0.12802996660612798,"bss_hi":-0.032762684984037095,"bss_lo":-0.2374391394326293,"chart":{"base":[532.7,282.5],"fp":[107.4,118.6],"lead":"62,242.7 272,237.4 482,228.5 692,210.3","note":{"base":"skill -0.13 — higher than 6% of cities","fp":"low end -7pp, high end +29pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.2 °C — better than 41% of cities","rel":"promised 36% → rained 22%; promised 99% → rained 74%"},"rel":"286.6,371.3 536.1,271.7 633.2,242.7 686.4,145.6"},"country":"MY","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.2604043126684637,"ess":517.1587982832624,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Kuala Lumpur</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Kuala Lumpur rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>76%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(20%), there is still roughly a <b>8%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 742 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nthe station, 15.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.13, ranked 203 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(194&ndash;205) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>8%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>51%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>70%</td><td class='num'><b>45%</b></td><td class='num'>77</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>81%</td><td class='num'><b>44%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>88%</td><td class='num'><b>58%</b></td><td class='num'>57</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>93%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>61</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>97%</td><td class='num'><b>68%</b></td><td class='num'>95</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>76%</b></td><td class='num'>234</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Kuala Lumpur</b> <span class=\"muted\">Malaysia</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;54% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 54% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.13</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>194&ndash;205\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>742 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Kuala Lumpur &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Kuala Lumpur\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"127.65323943661971,274.3380281690141 237.6904,153.89333333333332 305.11038961038963,93.63636363636363 344.98583333333335,58.44444444444446 370.2031578947369,37.15789473684214 387.1039344262295,23.967213114754088 401.6408421052631,18.0 411.78820512820516,18.0 411.78820512820516,19.555555555555543 401.6408421052631,40.98947368421051 387.1039344262295,71.7049180327869 370.2031578947369,94.63157894736844 344.98583333333335,119.11111111111114 305.11038961038963,164.54545454545456 237.6904,236.4 127.65323943661971,340.98591549295776\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"183.81132075471697\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"183.81132075471697\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"127.65323943661971,351.23943661971833 237.6904,255.81333333333333 305.11038961038963,216.54545454545456 344.98583333333335,220.22222222222223 370.2031578947369,171.26315789473682 387.1039344262295,214.91803278688525 401.6408421052631,132.94736842105263 411.78820512820516,103.5555555555556\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 8% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"127.65323943661971\" cy=\"351.23943661971833\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 51%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"237.6904\" cy=\"255.81333333333333\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 70%&amp;#10;It rained 45% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 77 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"305.11038961038963\" cy=\"216.54545454545456\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 81%&amp;#10;It rained 44% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"344.98583333333335\" cy=\"220.22222222222223\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 88%&amp;#10;It rained 58% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 57 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"370.2031578947369\" cy=\"171.26315789473682\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 93%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 61 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"387.1039344262295\" cy=\"214.91803278688525\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 97%&amp;#10;It rained 68% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 95 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"401.6408421052631\" cy=\"132.94736842105263\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 76% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 234 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.78820512820516\" cy=\"103.5555555555556\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(54%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Kuala Lumpur the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>autumn</b> (-0.00) and least in\n<b>spring</b> (-0.22).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>213</td><td class='num'>58%</td><td class='num'>-0.221</td><td class='num'>27.2%</td></tr><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>176</td><td class='num'>47%</td><td class='num'>-0.201</td><td class='num'>25.6%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>53%</td><td class='num'>-0.110</td><td class='num'>27.8%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>60%</td><td class='num'>-0.005</td><td class='num'>23.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":3.1412,"lon":101.68653,"n":742,"n_cities":216,"name":"Kuala Lumpur","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.39,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.19676056338028167,"n":71,"obs":0.08450704225352113,"sig":true},{"hi":0.63,"lo":0.39,"mean":0.5076,"n":75,"obs":0.3466666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":0.7630000000000005,"lo":0.63,"